      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/modules/configurations.ts",
      "supports": "Every method validates its identifier, places it as the only path segment of the matching endpoint and forwards any JSON payload unchanged. The two reads parse against ConfigurationGroupSchema and ConfigurationSchema; the two deletes resolve with no value."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-schema",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/schemas/configurations.ts",
      "supports": "ConfigurationGroupSchema carries id, name, project_id and a configs array; ConfigurationSchema carries id, name and group_id. The add payloads require name and the update payloads make it optional. No payload is parsed by the public method, which forwards it as given, so every payload rule is enforced at the MCP boundary alone."
    },
    {
      "id": "testrail-configurations",
      "url": "https://support.testrail.com/hc/en-us/articles/7077298488340-Configurations",
      "supports": "get_configs/{project_id} returns the configuration groups of a project, each with its configurations. add_config_group and add_config require a name; update_config_group and update_config take an optional name. Every one of these endpoints requires TestRail 5.2 or later. Deleting a group cannot be undone and removes every configuration in it; deleting either does not affect closed plans and runs, nor active ones until they are next updated."
    }
  ],
